From: Adn Elkawass <elkawasadn@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] aon-generate: drop O_DIRECT for small writes

aon-generate.sh writes small values while constructing the ELF header.
Using O_DIRECT for these writes can result in an incomplete ELF when the
helper is run during the BitBake build.

Drop oflag=direct and use normal buffered writes instead.

Upstream-Status: Pending [not yet submitted upstream]
AI-Generated: Uses OpenAI ChatGPT
Signed-off-by: Adn Elkawass <elkawasadn@gmail.com>
---
 aon-generate.sh | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/aon-generate.sh b/aon-generate.sh
--- a/aon-generate.sh
+++ b/aon-generate.sh
@@ -41 +41 @@
-	dd of="$outputFile" oflag=direct conv=notrunc bs=1 seek="$1" status=none
+	dd of="$outputFile" conv=notrunc bs=1 seek="$1" status=none
